          'SkillsetItemDelta::needsReEval() = added + updated ONLY. removed + reweighted NEVER call the LLM. scoringInputsChanged() = any change incl. reweight -> dispatchRecalcForDoneCandidates. Removed items: deleteRemovedItemRows drops the mirrored evaluation rows, no AI call.',
          'TWO persistence paths in SkillsetList.vue. (a) weight/threshold edits + gate<->criteria moves batch locally behind weightDirty and commit via POST /hiring-jobs/evaluation-policy/{job}/{skillset}/weight-versions. (b) add/delete/content-edit persist immediately via POST /hiring-jobs/evaluation-policy/{job}/{skillset}.',
          'blockIfWeightDirty(action) guards add/delete/content-edit/version-switch/reorder, PLUS accordion collapse/switch (toggleRow). Not arbitrary: buildCriterionPayload carries weight, so a structural save on a dirty board would write unversioned weights into the skillset JSON.',
          'Since 2026-08-09 those controls are DISABLED with an explanatory tooltip instead of accepting the click and toasting a refusal; tooltips sit on wrapper spans because a disabled button does not reliably emit the pointer events a tooltip trigger needs. Drag is stopped at the Sortable instance (:disabled on VueDraggable), not only in the drop handler. blockIfWeightDirty remains the backstop for paths that do not pass through a disabled control (drag-end, details save).',
          'toggleRow is guarded because Discard + Save-as-new-version render INSIDE the expanded body: collapsing a dirty board hid the only two controls that could resolve it while the slider went on refusing to close. Switching skillsets was worse, the skillsets.default watcher clears weightDirty outright.',
          'ONE slider since 2026-08-12: components/job/View.vue. The second implementation (components/app/JobView.vue) was deleted and app.vue now mounts job/View.vue and translates useJobViewer into props (:job_id + :defaultTab BEFORE v-model, because the open watcher is flush:sync and would otherwise fetch the previously viewed job). Both entry styles survive: 17 pages pass props, ~19 call sites write to the store.',
          'Unsaved-edit guarding covers close, tab change, the defaultTab watcher, the list pager and job_id retarget (the last was the one path that never asked, and it unmounts the board behind job.loading). The CLOSE path shows a three-way dialog (Keep editing / Discard changes / Save and close) calling the exposed saveUnsavedChanges; the other paths keep window.confirm because they need a boolean in the same tick. Confirming calls discardWeightEdits explicitly rather than relying on unmount.',
          'KNOWN GAP: a deletion is captured in NO version. createVersionLocked iterates the CURRENT EvaluationConfigItem rows, so once an item is deleted nothing references it and applyVersion cannot restore it. Also note omitting an item from the weights payload does NOT delete it, it falls back to weight 0.',
          'Save has no name modal (removed 2026-08-03): name is posted null so the server labels "Version N", and weightVersionLabel appends created_at so versions stay distinguishable without anyone typing.',
          'Job slider skillsets list sorts by the skillset\'s own created_at desc, id then original index as tiebreaks. Sorting is deliberately independent of tournaments: ordering by run recency buried a newly generated skillset under everything ever run.',
