          'Changing how a score is calculated is not the same as changing what is assessed.  Adjusting a weight or a threshold, moving an item between gates and criteria, or removing an item changes only the arithmetic, so candidate scores are recalculated in the background without asking the AI to read anything again.',
          'Adding an item, or editing the wording of an existing one, does change what is assessed.  Those items are re-evaluated by the AI in the background, and only the changed items are re-evaluated rather than the whole skillset.',
          'Weight and grouping edits are collected in the page and applied together when Save as new version is used.  Each save records a numbered version, and the version list shows the time each was saved so an earlier set of weights can be selected again.',
